          "heading": "Theoretical Framework: Flexure, Shear Stress and Beam Deflection",
          "content": "**Prerequisite knowledge:** force equilibrium, SI dimensional analysis, algebra and first-year calculus.\n\n**Learning objectives:** state a model and its validity range, calculate physically meaningful engineering quantities, reconcile equations with a free-body diagram or deformation compatibility, and identify at least two failure modes excluded by the idealization."
