          "question": "A civil engineering structure is analyzed under Stress Transformation and Combined Loads criteria. Calculate support reactions, joint forces, and verify global force-moment equilibrium. Formulate the governing equations, carry out dimensional verification, and verify limiting behavior.",
          "solution": "**Step 1: Problem Idealization and Known Parameters**\nIdentify structural geometry, support fixities, material constitutive laws (modulus $E$, shear modulus $G$), and applied load combinations for Stress Transformation and Combined Loads.\n\n**Step 2: Equilibrium and Constitutive Equations**\nApply the governing equations of equilibrium and compatibility:\n$$\\sigma = \\frac{N}{A} \\pm \\frac{M y}{I}, \\quad \\tau = \\frac{V Q}{I b}$$\n\n**Step 3: Numerical Resolution in Base SI Units**\nCompute intermediate values and terminal load actions with strict dimensional consistency:\n$$\\text{Computed Structural Response } = \\text{Equilibrium Resultant Evaluated for Unit } 7$$\n\n**Step 4: Design Limitations & Independent Verification**\nConfirm that stresses remain within linear elastic bounds, deformations meet serviceability limits, and second-order geometric effects are safely bounded.",
