          "content": "## Unit research project\n\nPrepare a technical notebook on **Columns, stability and geometric effects** for a civil engineering structure of your choice. Include a drawing with geometric dimensions, a carefully numbered input table and a free-body diagram. Develop two load or restraint scenarios, compute the most relevant stress or deformation variables, cross-check them with an independent limiting case, and identify all omissions that would prevent formal design approval. Where an associated laboratory exists, export a CSV series and include an annotated plot. Write a short conclusion that distinguishes what your simplified model genuinely predicts from what would need a professional code-based check.\n\n### Project marking rubric\n\n| Criterion | Suggested allocation |\n|---|---:|\n| Correct geometry, loads and units | 25% |\n| Equilibrium, constitutive law and compatibility | 25% |\n| Independent checks and model limitations | 25% |\n| Clear evidence, diagrams, reproducibility and communication | 25% |"
